{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If a user leaves your application and returns and the query data is stale, "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Query automatically requests fresh data for you in the background"}]},{"type":"text","value":". You can disable this globally or per-query using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"refetchOnWindowFocus"},{"type":"text","value":" option:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"disabling-globally","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Disabling Globally"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const appConfig: ApplicationConfig = {\n  providers: [\n    provideTanStackQuery(\n      new QueryClient({\n        defaultOptions: {\n          queries: {\n            refetchOnWindowFocus: false, // default: true\n          },\n        },\n      }),\n    ),\n  ],\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"disabling-per-query","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Disabling Per-Query"}]},{"type":"code","value":"injectQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['todos'],\n  queryFn: fetchTodos,\n  refetchOnWindowFocus: false,\n}))","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"custom-window-focus-event","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom Window Focus Event"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In rare circumstances, you may want to manage your own window focus events that trigger TanStack Query to revalidate. To do this, TanStack Query provides a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focusManager.setEventListener"},{"type":"text","value":" function that supplies you the callback that should be fired when the window is focused and allows you to set up your own events. When calling "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focusManager.setEventListener"},{"type":"text","value":", the previously set handler is removed (which in most cases will be the default handler) and your new handler is used instead. For example, this is the default handler:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"focusManager.setEventListener((handleFocus) => {\n  // Listen to visibilitychange\n  if (typeof window !== 'undefined' && window.addEventListener) {\n    const visibilitychangeHandler = () => {\n      handleFocus(document.visibilityState === 'visible')\n    }\n    window.addEventListener('visibilitychange', visibilitychangeHandler, false)\n    return () => {\n      // Be sure to unsubscribe if a new handler is set\n      window.removeEventListener('visibilitychange', visibilitychangeHandler)\n    }\n  }\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"managing-focus-state","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Managing focus state"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { focusManager } from '@tanstack/angular-query-experimental'\n\n// Override the default focus state\nfocusManager.setFocused(true)\n\n// Fallback to the default focus check\nfocusManager.setFocused(undefined)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"troubleshooting","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Troubleshooting"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If stale queries do not refetch when you return to a tab, check whether "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Emulate a focused page"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is enabled in Chrome DevTools. This setting keeps "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"document.visibilityState"},{"type":"text","value":" set to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"visible"},{"type":"text","value":" and prevents "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"visibilitychange"},{"type":"text","value":" events, which TanStack Query uses for its default focus handling."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Disable "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Emulate a focused page"}]},{"type":"text","value":" in the DevTools "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rendering"}]},{"type":"text","value":" panel, then switch to another tab and return to test window focus refetching. See the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://developer.chrome.com/docs/devtools/rendering/apply-effects#emulate_a_focused_page","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chrome DevTools documentation"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for more details."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"disabling-globally","text":"Disabling Globally","level":4},{"id":"disabling-per-query","text":"Disabling Per-Query","level":4},{"id":"custom-window-focus-event","text":"Custom Window Focus Event","level":2},{"id":"managing-focus-state","text":"Managing focus state","level":2},{"id":"troubleshooting","text":"Troubleshooting","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nIf a user leaves your application and returns and the query data is stale, **TanStack Query automatically requests fresh data for you in the background**. You can disable this globally or per-query using the `refetchOnWindowFocus` option:\n\n#### Disabling Globally\n\n\n\n```ts\nexport const appConfig: ApplicationConfig = {\n  providers: [\n    provideTanStackQuery(\n      new QueryClient({\n        defaultOptions: {\n          queries: {\n            refetchOnWindowFocus: false, // default: true\n          },\n        },\n      }),\n    ),\n  ],\n}\n```\n\n\n\n#### Disabling Per-Query\n\n\n\n```ts\ninjectQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['todos'],\n  queryFn: fetchTodos,\n  refetchOnWindowFocus: false,\n}))\n```\n\n\n\n## Custom Window Focus Event\n\nIn rare circumstances, you may want to manage your own window focus events that trigger TanStack Query to revalidate. To do this, TanStack Query provides a `focusManager.setEventListener` function that supplies you the callback that should be fired when the window is focused and allows you to set up your own events. When calling `focusManager.setEventListener`, the previously set handler is removed (which in most cases will be the default handler) and your new handler is used instead. For example, this is the default handler:\n\n\n\n```tsx\nfocusManager.setEventListener((handleFocus) => {\n  // Listen to visibilitychange\n  if (typeof window !== 'undefined' && window.addEventListener) {\n    const visibilitychangeHandler = () => {\n      handleFocus(document.visibilityState === 'visible')\n    }\n    window.addEventListener('visibilitychange', visibilitychangeHandler, false)\n    return () => {\n      // Be sure to unsubscribe if a new handler is set\n      window.removeEventListener('visibilitychange', visibilitychangeHandler)\n    }\n  }\n})\n```\n\n\n\n\n\n## Managing focus state\n\n\n\n```tsx\nimport { focusManager } from '@tanstack/angular-query-experimental'\n\n// Override the default focus state\nfocusManager.setFocused(true)\n\n// Fallback to the default focus check\nfocusManager.setFocused(undefined)\n```\n\n\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\nIf stale queries do not refetch when you return to a tab, check whether **Emulate a focused page** is enabled in Chrome DevTools. This setting keeps `document.visibilityState` set to `visible` and prevents `visibilitychange` events, which TanStack Query uses for its default focus handling.\n\nDisable **Emulate a focused page** in the DevTools **Rendering** panel, then switch to another tab and return to test window focus refetching. See the [Chrome DevTools documentation](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/devtools/rendering/apply-effects#emulate_a_focused_page) for more details.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: window-focus-refetching\ntitle: Window Focus Refetching\nref: docs/framework/react/guides/window-focus-refetching.md\nreplace: { '@tanstack/react-query': '@tanstack/angular-query-experimental' }\n---\n\n[//]: # 'Example'\n\n```ts\nexport const appConfig: ApplicationConfig = {\n  providers: [\n    provideTanStackQuery(\n      new QueryClient({\n        defaultOptions: {\n          queries: {\n            refetchOnWindowFocus: false, // default: true\n          },\n        },\n      }),\n    ),\n  ],\n}\n```\n\n[//]: # 'Example'\n[//]: # 'Example2'\n\n```ts\ninjectQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['todos'],\n  queryFn: fetchTodos,\n  refetchOnWindowFocus: false,\n}))\n```\n\n[//]: # 'Example2'\n[//]: # 'ReactNative'\n[//]: # 'ReactNative'\n"}
